Cut from main after the last three open items in docs/PATCHWORK_AUDIT.md were
finished. typecheck clean, 1,833 tests green, production build clean, `npm ci`
clean from an empty checkout with NO .npmrc, `bun install` clean, and the
screenshot sweep reports 63 screenshots / 0 problems.

VERSION NAME IS 1.2.6, NOT 1.2.5. Builds #90 and #91 both carried 1.2.5 and
NEITHER was promoted. This is different code, so it gets a different name —
two artefacts sharing a version string is how the Play Console, the crash
reports and the About screen stop agreeing with each other.

WHAT CHANGED SINCE #91

1. THE WEBSITE'S BUILD PATCH IS GONE, PROPERLY.
   When the site went dark for nine hours, `.npmrc legacy-peer-deps=true` was
   the hold that got it deploying again. A hold is not a cure: that flag tells
   npm to ignore peer conflicts ENTIRELY, so the next stale dependency would
   have hidden exactly the same way.
   react-day-picker is upgraded 8.10.1 -> 10.0.1, whose peer range genuinely
   accepts React 19, and **.npmrc is deleted**. Proved, not assumed:
   package.json + package-lock.json copied to an empty directory with no
   .npmrc, `npm ci` run there -> exit 0. GitHub's own clean checkout then
   agreed - 6/6 checks green.
   Bundle cost: none. 439.44 kB -> 439.42 kB gzipped.

2. EVERY TAP TARGET REACHES 44px.
   Feed 29 -> 0. Profile 17 -> 0. Post detail 14 -> 0. Login 2 -> 0.
   Notification settings 24 -> 0.
   Nothing was silenced to get there. The settings switches are the example
   worth knowing: instead of inflating the switch, the whole ROW is now the
   control - icon, title and description all toggle it, the way iOS and
   Android Settings work. The switch looks exactly as it did.

3. 33 TEST FILES NO LONGER CARRY A COMMENT STRIPPER THAT CAN DELETE REAL CODE.
   41 sites across 33 files now use the safe one. Two of the migrated tests
   were deliberately broken afterwards to confirm their alarms still fire.

